# Citation metadata (Citation File Format 1.2). GitHub shows it under "Cite this repository";
# Zenodo reads it when a GitHub release is archived. Update `version`, `date-released` and the
# DOI at every release; add ORCID iDs (https://orcid.org) to the authors.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SQANTI-evidence, please cite it using this metadata."
type: software
title: "SQANTI-evidence: structural genome annotation from long-read RNA-seq"
abstract: "Snakemake workflow that builds a structural genome annotation from a genome assembly and long-read RNA-seq (PacBio Iso-Seq/HiFi or Oxford Nanopore). Transcript models from IsoQuant are curated with SQANTI3 and written to the annotation unchanged (Tier 1); Augustus, trained on the species' own dominant ORFs and BUSCO orthologs and guided by hints from the curated transcripts and Miniprot self-protein alignments, fills the unexpressed loci (Tier 2)."
authors:
